# sentence_id = 114
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = If we have nothing better to say than what we've already said, know well that I will not agree with you, no, not even if the power of the majority should try to frighten us like children with more terrors than it now does — sending upon us bonds and death and confiscations of property.
# literal_translation = Of which [things], if we should not have better [things] to say in the present [circumstance], know well that I will certainly not agree with you — not even if the power of the many should frighten us, like [frightening] children, with more [terrors] than [those] now present, sending upon [us] bonds and deaths and confiscations of property.
