# prose_translation = Socrates: Isn't it so with the other matters as well, Crito, and especially so, in order that we may not go through them all—in matters of just and unjust, shameful and noble, good and bad, about which our present deliberation is—must we follow the opinion of the many, and fear it, or that of the one person, if there is someone who understands, whom we must respect and fear more than all the others together?
